{
  "_about": "This app's PRODUCTION chat flags, for the replay pack (src/app/api/chat/replay-pack). 'on': read as on in Vercel production. 'assumedOn': encrypted or not visible to the Vercel reader (it lists 100 of 181 entries), taken as on from QA's 26 Oct decrypted reading and the replays that match production. 'off': known off. QA messages every flag flipped; update this file in the same pull request as the change it tests. Only *_ENABLED chat flags; integrations (Woven, Google reviews) are left out. 5 Nov 2026 (QA; Pau's Vercel Agent read, 179 *_ENABLED rows, 49/49 plain values cross-checked against QA's API read): corrected to production — 5 assumedOn are OFF (CONVERSATION_DRAFT_REUSE, DRAFT_ACTIONS, GROUNDED_ENTITIES, PROMPT_CACHE, REMAP_DRAFT_SOURCES), 2 'off' are ON (ANSWER_NOT_A_NAME, STORE_WORD_NOT_A_NAME), 48 ON flags were missing; the explicit OFF values are listed in 'off'. SELF_CHECK_ENABLED is unset in Vercel (= off) and stays in 'off'. WOVEN_SYNC_WRITES is left out (sensitive). Why the (a) flags are off (Vercel comments, QA's read-only reader): GROUNDED_ENTITIES was set back to 0 on 24 Oct ~9:38 PM Manila, a deliberate rollback (it dropped non-roster names while ANTI_LOOP was off); CONVERSATION_DRAFT_REUSE and DRAFT_ACTIONS were rolled back 25 Oct (B18/B19: they reopened or overwrote another chat's draft); PROMPT_CACHE was off 25 Oct (no speed gain); SLOT_RETENTION was rolled back 24 Oct (Job Title bug). 5 Nov 2026, the smaller flip (QA; read from Vercel at 06:52 PHT): CA_SALES_POLICY_ENABLED, REPLY_MATCHES_CARD_ENABLED, TITLE_OF_THE_EMPLOYEE_ENABLED and METRIC_GUARD_ENABLED are ON; the name flags (FORM_NAME_FROM_ROSTER, ROSTER_NEAR_MISS, ROSTER_NAME_IN_CANDIDATE, ROSTER_COMPOUND_SURNAME, ROSTER_NOT_FOUND_ANY_PHRASING) stay off. 6 Nov 2026, flip 3 (QA; on a clean gate rerun 4 on 87c08239, docs/flag-classification/FLIP3D.md): FORM_NAME_FROM_ROSTER, ROSTER_NEAR_MISS, ROSTER_NAME_IN_CANDIDATE, ROSTER_COMPOUND_SURNAME, ROSTER_NOT_FOUND_ANY_PHRASING, POLIC